      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In a prospective pilot study on 100 consecutive patients with symptomatic cholelithiasis the laparoscopic cholecystectomy shows to be a safe technic without mortality and a low complication rate (3%). The time of operation is influenced by a learning curve of the operation-team and depends on the technical equipment. The postoperative hospital stay is 3 days in median. Postoperatively the pain-intensity is low and decreased very fast. These increased the patients perioperative comfort."},
